/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 121 0 R
/T (The code uses train_test_split with test_size=0.20 and random_state=42. Approximately 80% of the records \(800\) are used for model fitting and 20% \(200\) are held out for evaluation. random_state=42 makes the split reproducible when the data and settings remain unchanged. The split is not stratified, so the class proportions in the test set can differ slightly from the full dataset: the test set contains 61 approved and 139 not-approved applications \(30.5% approved\). )
/E (The code uses train_test_split with test_size=0.20 and random_state=42. Approximately 80% of the records \(800\) are used for model fitting and 20% \(200\) are held out for evaluation. random_state=42 makes the split reproducible when the data and settings remain unchanged. The split is not stratified, so the class proportions in the test set can differ slightly from the full dataset: the test set contains 61 approved and 139 not-approved applications \(30.5% approved\). )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
