417 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 126 0 R
/T (In this project, approval is treated as the positive class. A false negativeisanapplicant who should have been approved but was predicted as not approved, which is a missedbusiness opportunity. A false positive is an applicant who was predicted as approved but should not havebeen, which is the more costly error for a lender because it exposes the bank to default risk. The modelmakes 3 false negatives and 10 false positives. )
/E (In this project, approval is treated as the positive class. A false negativeisanapplicant who should have been approved but was predicted as not approved, which is a missedbusiness opportunity. A false positive is an applicant who was predicted as approved but should not havebeen, which is the more costly error for a lender because it exposes the bank to default risk. The modelmakes 3 false negatives and 10 false positives. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
