/Title (In this project, approval is treated as the positive class. A false negativeisanapplicant who should have been approved but was predicted as not approved, which is a missedbusiness opportunity. A false positive is an applicant who was predicted as approved but should not havebeen, which is the more costly error for a lender because it exposes the bank to default risk. The modelmakes 3 false negatives and 10 false positives.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 684 0 R
/Next 767 0 R
>>
