827 0 obj
<<
/Title (The tuned XGBoost model has the best accuracy \(93.5%\), recall \(95.1%\) and F1-score \(89.9%\). It correctly identifies 58 of the 61 approved applications. Its precision of 85.3% means that about 15% of the applications it predicts as approved would not have been approved, which matters because wrongly approved loans carry credit risk. Tuning raised recall from 91.8% to 95.1% but lowered precision slightly from 86.2% to 85.3%. With only 200 test records, one record changes accuracy by 0.5 points, so the gaps between the top ensemble models are small and should not be over-interpreted.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 810 0 R
/Prev 826 0 R
>>
